 "text": "-->\nAg Plus, Inc. - Department: Grain\n-->\nDepartment: Grain\nToggle Navigation\nHome\nAbout Ag Plus -->\nAbout Ag Plus\nMeet our Team\nHistory of Ag Plus\nAbout Ag Plus\nDivisions -->\nDivisions\nAgronomy\nEnergy\nFeed\nGrain\nTurf\nLocations & Hours\nResources -->\nResources\nAg Plus Credit Application\nSynergy Credit Application\nSafety\nLocal Weather\nCustomer Portal -->\nCustomer Portal\nAg Plus\nSynergy Feed\nContact Us -->\nContact Us\nCall\nEmail\nEmployee Resources\nEmployment Opportunities\nAg Plus Precision\nAg Plus Scholarship\nConnect\n-->\nPrevious\nNext\n-->\n-->\n-->\n-->\n|\n-->\n-->\n-->\n-->\nOctober 16, 2026\nCorn export sales were in the upper portion of the trade’s expectations at 44.2 mbu vs. 20 – 47 mbu estimated and below the 52.2 needed. December corn futures settled .04 cnets lower on the day at $7.47 ¼ and now hovers just above the 300 DMA. March 27 contract is down -.04 ½ cents at $4.86 ½.\nSoybean export sales came in at 21.1 mbu vs. 18 – 44 expected with flash sales of 558 KMT to China and 236 KMT to unknown destinations. November 26 soybean futures settle nearly .02 cents lower at $12.61 ¼ with the January 2027 contract down -.02 cents at $12.75 ¾.\nDecember wheat was down -.09 ½ cents at $6.60 ½ with the July 27 contract down -.07 cents at $6.83 ¼.\nSouth Whitley - 260-723-5141\nRaber - 260-244-5188\nBusco - 260-693-2161\nGarrett - 260-357-5432\nMonroeville - 260-623-6121\nEdgerton - 260-632-4284\n-->\n-->\nAt Ag Plus, we understand the hard work that goes into every harvest. That's why we're committed to serving our grain customers with integrity, experience, and service you can count on. We offer competitive grain bids on corn, soybeans, and wheat, personalized pricing programs, and direct access to real time grain pricing near you, so you get the most value for your grain.\nOur dedicated team is here to support your operation with dependable transportation, drying, and storage solutions. During harvest, we take pride in unloading your grain quickly to help you avoid bottlenecks and keep things running smoothly.\nWhether you're marketing corn, soybeans, or wheat, we’re here to make the process easier, more profitable, and more personal. If you have questions or want to talk through your options, please reach out to our team! Click to contact!\nOur Grain Staff\nVP of Grain\nBrian Leydens\nLocation Managers\nLarry Coomer |\nGrain Originator Edgerton |\nLaura Grime |\nGrain Originator South Whitley |\nMark Marshall |\nGrain Originator South Whitley |\nRyan Brown |\nGrain Originator South Whitley |\n|\n|\nBrian Jordan |\nMonroeville Location Manager |\nDustin Bennett |\nGarrett Location Manager |\nPhil Williams |\nEdgerton Location Manager |\nClayton Badskey |\nChurubusco Location Manager |\nJim Eiler |\nRaber Location Manager |\n-->\n-->\nGrain Locations\nAt Ag Plus, we proudly serve farmers across Northeast Indiana and Northwest Ohio with trusted and convenient Grain Services.\nWe offer grain contracts, grain marketing services, and access to competitive local grain bids to help you maximize the value of your harvest.\nBelow are our Ag Plus grain locations, each linked for easy directions and contact:\nWhether you need help with selling grain, securing competitive prices, or finding the right grain marketing plan, Ag Plus is here to help.\nCall or visit your nearest Ag Plus grain location today.\nChurubusco Ag Center\n|\nEdgerton Grain\n|\nMonroeville Grain\n|\nMap\n9325 E State Rd. 205 Churubusco, IN 46723\n(260) 693-2161\nHours: Monday-Friday 7:30am-5pm Saturday 7:30am-12pm\nAgronomy, Grain, Feed\n|\nMap\n1519 Everson Rd Woodburn, IN 46797\n(260) 632-4284\nHours: Monday-Friday8am-4:30pm Saturday Seasonal Hours\nGrain\n|\nMap\n306 W South St. PO Box 504 Monroeville, IN 46773\n(260) 623-6121\nHours: Monday-Friday 8am-4:30pm Saturday Seasonal Hours\nGrain\n|\n|\n|\n|\nRaber Ag Center\n|\nSouth Whitley Ag Center\n|\nGarrett Ag Center (& Rail)\n|\nMap\n5480 South Raber Road Columbia City, IN 46725\n(260) 244-5188\nHours: Monday-Friday 7:30am-5pm Saturday 7:30am-12pm\nAgronomy, Grain, Feed, Turf\n|\nMap\n401 North Main PO Box 306 South Whitley, IN 46787\n(260) 723-5141\nHours: Monday-Friday 7:30am-5pm Saturday Seasonal Hours\nAgronomy, Grain, Synergy Feeds\n|\nMap\n2006 County Rd 48 Garrett, IN 46738\n(260) 357-5432\nHours: Monday-Friday 7:30am-5pm Saturday Seasonal Hours\nGrain, Agronomy, Feed, Turf\n|\n|\n|\n|\nChurubusco Ag Center\nMap\n9325 E State Rd. 205 Churubusco, IN 46723\n(260) 693-2161\nHours: Monday-Friday 7:30am-5pm Saturday 7:30am-12pm\nAgronomy, Grain, Feed\n|\nEdgerton Grain\nMap\n1519 Everson Rd Woodburn, IN 46797\n(260) 632-4284\nHours: Monday-Friday8am-4:30pm Saturday Seasonal Hours\nGrain,\n|\nMonroeville Grain\nMap\n306 W South St. PO Box 504 Monroeville, IN 46773\n(260) 623-6121\nHours: Monday-Friday 8am-4:30pm Saturday Seasonal Hours\nGrain\n|\nRaber Ag Center\nMap\n5480 South Raber Road Columbia City, IN 46725\n(260) 244-5188\nHours: Monday-Friday 7:30am-5pm Saturday 7:30am-12pm\nAgronomy, Grain, Feed, Turf\n|\nSouth Whitley Ag Center\nMap\n401 North Main PO Box 306 South Whitley, IN 46787\n(260) 723-5141\nHours: Monday-Friday 7:30am-5pm Saturday Seasonal hours\nAgronomy, Grain, Synergy Feeds\n|\nGarrett Ag Center (& Rail)\nMap\n2006 County Rd 48 Garrett, IN 46738\n(260) 357-5432\nHours: Monday-Friday 7:30am-5pm Saturday Seasonal Hours\nGrain, Agronomy, Feed, Turf\n|\n-->\nCash Bids\nMarket Center\nA Day in the Life of an Ag Plus Truck Driver\nWanting to learn how to manage Vomitoxin??\nClick on the link below to find the video!\nCorn School Managing Vomitoxin\nSeptember 5, 2025 We would like to encourage our grain customers to sign up for ACH payments on grain. Postal rates continue to climb, service conti\n-->\n|\n|\n|\n|\n-->\n-->\nHarvest 2025\n|\n|\n|\n|\n|\n|\n|\n|\n|\n|\n|\n|\n|\n|\n|\n|\n|\n|\n|\n|\n|\n|\n|\n|\n|\n|\n|\n|\n|\n|\n-->\n© 2026 Barchart.com, Inc. All market data is hosted and powered by Barchart .\nInformation presented is provided 'as-is' and solely for informational purposes, not for trading purposes or advice, and is delayed. No representations are made by Barchart as to its informational accuracy or completeness.\nTerms of Use\nPrivacy Policy\nDo Not Sell My Personal Information\nExchange Delays\nBy using this site, you agree to the storage of cookies on your devices for enhanced navigation, site analysis, and Barchart's marketing. Data sharing with social media platforms might occur based on the privacy choices you make on those platforms. For specifics, see our our Privacy Policy .\nAccept",
